 matrix is upper triangular, so it is our matrix $U.$ Now, since ${E}_{1}A=U,$ we can invert ${E}_{1}$ to arrive at the desired LU factorization:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{E}_{1}A & =U \\\\ A & ={E}_{1}^{-1}U \\\\ A & ={\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1}U \\\\ A & ={{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{L}{{\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{U}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186402054 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eab33316-9a2a-5e12-b51c-b02a826d1b0c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402056} {:answer/id #uuid "1bad7312-2e66-5700-9aae-eb7c85b9c383" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the listed" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402057} {:answer/id #uuid "7f572362-82aa-5062-a6d6-241eb9bbaaef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 18 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402058} {:answer/id #uuid "a48759ab-5bd7-525d-8ee8-1aa323ee45c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 32\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402059} {:answer/id #uuid "55aa56c5-1a06-51f3-9787-5f99d9d8585f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402060}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402060} :answer-field/id #uuid "1f4ecb30-087b-5664-9448-53b7642eb521" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402055}] :question/id #uuid "c7e3bf80-d71d-502c-8977-ed540b710cc2" :question/math-academy-id "q-32608" :question/problem "Given that  $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 \\\\ -5 & -7\\end{bmatrix}$ has the LU decomposition $