ac{2}{3},$ ${u}_{22}=0,$ and ${l}_{21}+{u}_{22}=-\\frac{2}{3}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302246 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "313f7f73-ae71-5493-992f-4e48bea91c88" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300201} {:answer/id #uuid "31938138-7d2c-5bed-930a-21cc179190f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300205} {:answer/id #uuid "b073af7e-07ec-5fcd-bbd1-bcce7e503f63" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300842} {:answer/id #uuid "c1d443bc-9fc8-52e6-ab7c-4ece0d4276c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300937} {:answer/id #uuid "eea969a6-a2e5-502c-8add-7b9d6854171a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301144}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300937} :answer-field/id #uuid "bb7be8c1-9dd6-5e40-801c-bb8c984dfe84" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301841}] :question/id #uuid "54aa3fc3-c0fb-5a79-b3e0-2e2c9dd3e2c8" :question/math-academy-id "q-32597" :question/problem "Given that \n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -6\\end{bmatrix}$\nhas the LU decomposition $A=LU$, then ${l}_{21}+{u}_{22}=$" :question/worked-solution "We need to reduce the matrix to the row echelon form. For every elementary row operation we also write the equivalent notation in terms of multiplication by the corresponding elementary matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -6\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1}\\,⟺\\,\\overset{{E}_{1}}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}}\\cdot A \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =U\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix is upper triangular, so it is our matrix $U.$ Now, since ${E}_{1}A=U,$ we can invert ${E}_{1}$ to arrive at the desired LU factorization:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{E}_{1}A & =U \\\\ A & ={E}_{1}^{-1}U \\\\ A & ={\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1}U \\\\ A & ={{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{L}{{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{U}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${l}_{21}=-2,{u}_{22}=0,$ and ${l}_{21}+{u}_{22}=-2.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345039 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09bc7317-06c8-5646-a319-6454ce262a74" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342318} {:answer/id #uuid "25543171-560e-5885-8cbf-95ea1baa9696" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342552} {:answer/id #uuid "3ba87d52-95c1-597d-9b2e-c70531a0669c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342728} {:answer/id #uuid "599a0e0b-3bc3-52dd-bbce-2d68e327be82" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342990} {:answer/id #uuid "66e6279e-9fdc-59cd-982a-b9a4a5f0030b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343111}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342318} :answer-field/id #uuid "2157e8d4-ef66-5551-92f1-23781372ee67" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344552}] :question/id #uuid "6f2e5b5a-5004-55c2-853e-21858f1d4855" :question/math-academy-id "q-75179" :question/problem "Given that $A=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -2 \\\\ 9 & 6\\end{bmatrix}$\nhas the LU decomposition $A=LU$, then ${l}_{21}+{u}_{22}=$" :question/worked-solution "To find the matrices $L$ and $U,$ we reduce the matrix $A$ to row echelon form. Whilst doing this, we simultaneously write down the 