reduced matrix is upper triangular, so it is our matrix $U.$ Now, since ${E}_{1}A=U,$ we can invert ${E}_{1}$ to arrive at the desired LU factorization:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{E}_{1}A & =U \\\\ A & ={E}_{1}^{-1}U \\\\ A & ={\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1}U \\\\ A & ={{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{L}{{\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{U}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${l}_{21}=-3,$ ${u}_{22}=0,$ and ${l}_{21}+{u}_{22}=-3.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186555769 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25d6bf9d-c36b-57f4-a4a3-d6d10d20a9fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555078} {:answer/id #uuid "2d113435-7d4d-5e64-bf7a-6096265af4ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555100} {:answer/id #uuid "97a99f95-7b5c-511f-b1dd-63628675fb7e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555361} {:answer/id #uuid "ac5ab758-9dd9-5005-99ab-90aa7d7d9c95" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555414} {:answer/id #uuid "b15e8623-fcd9-53a6-8695-28d9aee82949" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555427}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555414} :answer-field/id #uuid "89806148-2b04-5dff-9c9d-9aecabad8125" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555707}] :question/id #uuid "1cf3361e-986e-5750-bf9f-73762dff3b0e" :question/math-academy-id "q-106771" :question/problem "Given that\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -8 \\\\ -1 & -4\\end{aligned}]$\nhas the LU decomposition $A=LU$, then ${l}_{21}+{u}_{22}=$" :question/worked-solution "To find the matrices $L$ and $U,$ we reduce the matrix $A$ to row echelon form. Whilst doing this, we simultaneously write down the row operations applied to $A$ in terms of matrix multiplication using elementary matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -8 \\\\ -1 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-\\frac{1}{2}){R}_{1}\\,⟺\\,\\overset{{E}_{1}}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} & 1\\end{aligned}]}}\\cdot A \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =U\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix is upper triangular, so it is our matrix $U.$ Now, since ${E}_{1}A=U,$ we can invert ${E}_{1}$ to arrive at the desired LU factorization:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{E}_{1}A & =U \\\\ A & ={E}_{1}^{-1}U \\\\ A & ={[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} & 1\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}U \\\\ A & ={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{L}{{[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{U}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${l}_{21}=\\frac{1}{2},$ ${u}_{22}=0,$ and ${l}_{21}+{u}_{22}=\\frac{1}{2}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186555856 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d7c47e5-bc18-5759-9dba-bef203ec6a76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555101} {:answer/id #uuid "382d6998-098c-5ac8-a4eb-2cf87144df8e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555121} {:answer/id #uuid "49cdf79c-58f3-5591-94f0-0d48ea2d4f6c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555158} {:answer/id #uuid "4da3e47c-22f5-5965-908e-6f3b266993d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555174} {:answer/id #uuid "c847da6e-0099-5446-9b32-bda4703a56ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555480}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555158} :answer-field/id #uuid "3bb19108-7f19-5591-ae3c-6544894088fe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555669}] :question/id #uuid "d20ab7a7-2299-5eca-8c7e-9709ddaf034c" :question/math-academy-id "q-32547" :question/problem "Given that\n $A=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ -12 & -9\\end{aligned}]$ \nhas the LU decomposition $A=LU$, then ${l}_{21}+{u}_{22}=$" :question/worked-solution "To find the matrices $L$ and $U,$ we reduce the matrix $A$ to row echelon form. Whilst doing this, we simultaneously write down the row operations applied to $A$ in terms of matrix multiplication using elementary matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ -12 & -9\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1}\\,⟺\\,\\overset{{E}_{1}}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]}}\\cdot A \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =U\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix is upper triangular, so it is our matrix $U.$ Now, since ${E}_{1}A=U,$ we can invert ${E}_{1}$ to arrive at the desired LU factorization:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{E}_{1}A & =U \\\\ A & ={E}_{1}^{-1}U \\\\ A & ={[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}U \\\\ A & ={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{L}{{[\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{U}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${l}_{21}=-3,{u}_{22}=0,$ and ${l}_{21}+{u}_{22}=-3.$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the LU Factorization of a Singular 2x2 Matrix"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119853 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119668 :question/id #uuid "ea39d5ec-9c8f-572d-8708-fdd97d0c04bc" :question/math-academy-id "e-6184" :question/problem "Which of the following products is the LU factorization of a matrix $A?$\n\nI. ![](images/62/62e90ac708f5a7d2942d328a1dcbcfc435e6cf900b71f0564307e020d822748b.svg)\n\nII. ![](images/94/94db4ea75dacbd6aaf0ab0e32a6f871bc6e50c8029da7c6800a49762feb2f560.svg)\n\nIII. ![](images/e4/e4b8dd6cb97a21581eb6d2cc2ddcd6028917aeff8d76cd55185acb995ff3074c.svg)" :question/worked-solution "Remember that in the LU factorization of a matrix $A,$ we write $A=LU$ where the matrix $L$ is a unit lower triangular matrix (a lower triangular matrix that has only $1$'s on the main diagonal) and the matrix $U$ is an upper triangular matrix:\n\n![](images/e1/e1b3730913029ed000c4ef86338bcd8be0fff045cda12131f894a1818996521b.svg)\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each product in turn.\n\n- The first product is in $LU$ form because the left matrix is a unit lower triangular matrix, and the right matrix is an upper triangular matrix.\n![](images/a7/a7d5c905d9f78444b00c51a1b641d132365f5fc8619ad00fc0fd5fc27942709c.svg)\n\n- The second product is *not* in $LU$ form. Although the left matrix is a lower triangular matrix, it is not a *unit* lower triangular matrix because it does not have $1$'s on the diagonal.\n![](images/f1/f1d0656f8aabffd2d3e2bee903f3763aa610a4731991669a625e473262d7ea32.svg)\n\n- The third product is *not* in $LU$ form because the matrix on the right is not an upper triangular matrix, as it has a non-zero entry below the diagonal.\n![](images/00/00c52c08ef614e87fe29584d994cec16298fa1f3bf02a1b4c6b7463bede7a6d1.svg)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c2c1a562-1b3d-5180-9fef-e20ea916b17a" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120188 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "252ce171-0755-52d0-8ca8-2eb206da07f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477215} {:answer/id #uuid "c64c0d42-e243-5c96-a744-1ef7c6890992" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477216}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477215} :answer-field/id #uuid "9df02e3d-de8c-5154-9f5d-c1801992c64b" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477577} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f7ab7a70-5a28-59e2-955b-0681d218bfef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477217} {:answer/id #uuid "a4aa48c4-2113-52f8-984d-4a71a2c2ff9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477218}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477217} :answer-field/id #uuid "b0c08f72-5093-5b6b-bc41-a096269ec2aa" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477578} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a3fb7b08-d488-58e2-980c-afd54977ad4d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477219} {:answer/id #uuid "ada4624e-8ffe-5859-8294-a52aec7585c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477220}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477220} :answer-field/id #uuid "f2ab1b30-8062-5c91-b5bc-ff9c735581fc" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477579}] :question/id #uuid "85de5a76-468b-557f-8cba-f675615513a3" :question/math-academy-id "q-32551" :question/problem "Which of the following products is the LU factorization of a matrix $A?$\n\nI. $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nII. $A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nIII. $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Remember that in the LU factorization of a matrix $A,$ we write $A=LU$ where the matrix $L$ is a unit lower triangular matrix (a lower triangular matrix that has only $1$'s on the main diagonal) and the matrix $U$ is an upper triangular matrix:\n\n$$\nA=\\overset{L}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ ∗ & 1\\end{bmatrix}}}\\cdot \\overset{U}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}∗ & ∗ \\\\ 0 & ∗\\end{bmatrix}}}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each product in turn.\n\n- The first product is *not* in $LU$ form because the matrix on the right is not an upper triangular matrix, as it has a non-zero entry below the diagonal.\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\,\\times \n$$\n\n- The second product is *not* in $LU$ form. Although we have a product of an upper triangular matrix on the left and a unit lower triangular matrix on the right, the order of multiplication is not correct (instead, we need a unit lower triangular matrix on the left and an upper triangular matrix on the right).\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\,\\times \n$$\n\n- The third product is in $LU$ form because the left matrix is a unit lower triangular matrix, and the right matrix is an upper triangular matrix.\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\,✓\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120197 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8308f719-9c9e-531e-a4ec-97b68e8d606a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117344} {:answer/id #uuid "8ec51409-e984-55df-bf9a-2a9287757947" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117345} {:answer/id #uuid "e3cf7197-0f7d-5fc8-aada-e25be5df7772" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117346} {:answer/id #uuid "ef5ad70c-88b9-59a4-bfa6-56e20fb74875" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117347} {:answer/id #uuid "178010b4-23ca-597f-821e-15b0495bd5a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117348}] :answer-field/id #uuid "2a1940e4-e4ff-5b03-a880-1641fc437faa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117343}] :question/id #uuid "9e468a23-8ad5-5652-8aab-04e323c7e93b" :question/math-academy-id "q-32607" :question/problem "Which of the following products is the LU factorization of a matrix $A$?\n\n1. $A = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 7 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$\n2. $A = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 7 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}9 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$\n3. $A = \\begin{bmatrix}9 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 7 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186243945 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "56258d8c-e646-509a-8f28-9b491b3481fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461455} {:answer/id #uuid "09ef23d4-862d-578f-b427-bbae133ead4a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461456}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461456} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b2d6e88-66be-55b8-937a-f097cf9d0a8f" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462481} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ae5b49c3-0779-557c-8921-65282b453bed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461457} {:answer/id #uuid "68c311fa-d65a-5064-a5f2-843e88a9f3f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461458}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461457} :answer-field/id #uuid "0fdefae0-1945-5459-8e2f-89ff965eadc8" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462482} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "41c731b3-dbc9-5242-b984-177958f91d5e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461459} {:answer/id #uuid "6bd0f37d-448b-5552-acb3-dff3d5f8c125" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461460}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461459} :answer-field/id #uuid "4715c2ce-c869-5eb5-8141-1dcbba399ac8" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462483}] :question/id #uuid "ae199b8f-96fc-541b-8e00-25e26e1c8f40" :question/math-academy-id "q-106751" :question/problem "Which of the following products is the LU factorization of a matrix $A?$\n- **I.** $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}$\n- **II.** $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}$\n- **III.** $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that in the LU factorization of a matrix $A,$ we write $A=LU$ where the matrix $L$ is a unit lower triangular matrix (a lower triangular matrix that has only $1$'s on the main diagonal) and the matrix $U$ is an upper triangular matrix:\n\n$$\nA=\\overset{L}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ ∗ & 1\\end{bmatrix}}}\\cdot \\overset{U}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}∗ & ∗ \\\\ 0 & ∗\\end{bmatrix}}}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each product in turn.\n\n- The first product is in $LU$ form because the left matrix is a unit lower triangular matrix, and the right matrix is an upper triangular matrix.\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\,✓\n$$\n\n- The second product is *not* in $LU$ form because the matrix on the left is not a unit lower triangular matrix, as its main diagonal contains a number not equal to $1.$\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\,\\times \n$$\n\n- The third product is *not* in $LU$ form because the matrix on the right is not an upper triangular matrix, as it has a non-zero entry below the diagonal.\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\,\\times \n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186243947 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fe57a78b-d4ad-58a3-a332-1d5d1a41161f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461461} {:answer/id #uuid "ed276dc2-e752-5149-8daa-6a78dac6eb3c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461462}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461461} :answer-field/id #uuid "8ad862c7-06d6-5d3e-9df8-9dc54efcf0c4" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462484} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "553c272d-3d3a-5260-bd9f-714a8605af98" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461463} {:answer/id #uuid "4e234d92-1a15-5982-80b2-1a67952674f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461464}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461464} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a44ba0a-420a-5ce8-9090-7717c7cae446" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462485} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b2f54ad7-e111-5f33-a28c-2b1e1910a1da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461465} {:answer/id #uuid "90d8b03d-a3ca-513c-a593-4303a50bda9a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461466}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461466} :answer-field/id #uuid "b7e2bb08-94b2-5ba1-8d6a-ae59c5114f74" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462486}] :question/id #uuid "02d764cc-1d89-57be-9543-a3cb1c6ba444" :question/math-academy-id "q-106756" :question/problem "Which of the following products is the LU factorization of a matrix $A?$\n- **I.** $A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$\n- **II.** $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}$\n- **III.** $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that in the LU factorization of a matrix $A,$ we write $A=LU$ where the matrix $L$ is a unit lower triangular matrix (a lower triangular matrix that has only $1$'s on the main diagonal) and the matrix $U$ is an upper triangular matrix:\n\n$$\nA=\\overset{L}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ ∗ & 1\\end{bmatrix}}}\\cdot \\overset{U}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}∗ & ∗ \\\\ 0 & ∗\\end{bmatrix}}}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each product in turn.\n\n- The first product is *not* in $LU$ form because the matrix on the left is not a unit lower triangular matrix, as its main diagonal contains a number not equal to $1.$\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\,\\times \n$$\n\n- The second product is in $LU$ form because the left matrix is a unit lower triangular matrix, and the right matrix is an upper triangular matrix.\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\,✓\n$$\n\n- The third product is in $LU$ form because the left matrix is a unit lower triangular matrix, and the right matrix is an upper triangular matrix.\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\,✓\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345029 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3aff888b-3abd-519a-b020-976dc34f4245" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468100} {:answer/id #uuid "25a7ba29-bc65-581b-9964-6c11c222d79f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468101}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468100} :answer-field/id #uuid "4f47bd49-5b77-5103-8d2d-487667211ef5" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468771} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7cbf7e8b-34e0-5ba3-bf96-0aa8c395b97b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468102} {:answer/id #uuid "a74eb240-f723-5f61-8cdf-f327609c7cf2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468103}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468102} :answer-field/id #uuid "1002dbbd-d4c2-58a4-9d7a-a603394b05ab" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468772} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "323a7811-4035-5802-b65f-fa37ee80f272" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468104} {:answer/id #uuid "6196d8dc-3375-5b48-89b1-f58fc5a8344c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468105}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468105} :answer-field/id #uuid "3c3ed68e-ffbd-5c3c-9b32-90b080f28a48" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468773}] :question/id #uuid "89a636cd-a216-5d73-bd3f-7f9cbe4badf4" :question/math-academy-id "q-75116" :question/problem "Which of the following products is the LU factorization of a matrix $C?$\n- **I.** $C=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$\n- **II.** $C=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$\n- **III.** $C=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that in the LU factorization of a matrix $C,$ we write $C=LU$ where the matrix $L$ is a unit lower triangular matrix (a lower triangular matrix that has only $1$'s on the main diagonal) and the matrix $U$ is an upper triangular matrix:\n\n$$\nC=\\overset{L}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ ∗ & 1\\end{bmatrix}}}\\cdot \\overset{U}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}∗ & ∗ \\\\ 0 & ∗\\end{bmatrix}}}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each product in turn.\n\n- The first product is *not* in $LU$ form  because  the matrix on the left is not a unit lower triangular matrix, as its main diagonal contains a number not equal to $1.$\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\,\\times \n$$\n\n- The second product is *not* in $LU$ form. Although we have a product of an upper triangular matrix on the left and a unit lower triangular matrix on the right, the order of multiplication is not correct (instead, we need a unit lower triangular matrix on the left and an upper triangular matrix on the right).\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\,\\times \n$$\n\n- The third product is in $LU$ form because the left matrix is a unit lower triangular matrix, and the right matrix is an upper triangular matrix. \n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\,✓\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345030 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9e49e90f-76ff-5359-a83b-d19ac304cc98" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468106} {:answer/id #uuid "10dda677-3970-5dca-925d-f1fd92be396a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468107}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468106} :answer-field/id #uuid "c64d7a54-ae7c-59e3-b98f-bb2beec3e574" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468774} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0861ba46-156e-530e-b250-d70406ef7823" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468108} {:answer/id #uuid "2ceee5b2-6950-50cb-8401-965ea76654fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468109}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468108} :answer-field/id #uuid "2077df0d-33ac-5ccf-9556-c6e7cc2502c2" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468775} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "49ff15f0-f00d-52b8-b7dc-4e1b5d1b9bde" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468110} {:answer/id #uuid "c91cd91b-5643-5712-a070-3652a02db457" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468111}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468111} :answer-field/id #uuid "0accbf5a-ff99-5165-88e6-f3ee36af91b4" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468776}] :question/id #uuid "0305a43d-bf81-5ecb-8a77-49a30ade0147" :question/math-academy-id "q-75117" :question/problem "Which of the following products is the LU factorization of a matrix $A?$\n\nI. $A=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nII. $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nIII. $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that in the LU factorization of a matrix $A,$ we write $A=LU$ where the matrix $L$ is a unit lower triangular matrix (a lower triangular matrix that has only $1$'s on the main diagonal) and the matrix $U$ is an upper triangular matrix:  \n\n$$\nA=\\overset{L}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ ∗ & 1\\end{bmatrix}}}\\cdot \\overset{U}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}∗ & ∗ \\\\ 0 & ∗\\end{bmatrix}}}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each product in turn.\n\n- The first product is *not* in $LU$ form because the matrix on the left is not a unit lower triangular matrix, as it has an entry not equal to $1$  on the main diagonal.\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\,\\times \n$$\n\n- The second product is *not* in $LU$ form because the matrix on the right is not an upper triangular matrix, as it has a non-zero entry below the diagonal. \n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\,\\times \n$$\n\n- The third product is in $LU$ form because the left matrix is a unit lower triangular matrix, and the right matrix is an upper triangular matrix.\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\,✓\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345033 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "62ddc631-4c21-5b83-858a-b840b32aee4f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468112} {:answer/id #uuid "d8b9dd2e-47fe-5d22-ae99-25d7bbdf4e05" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468113}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468113} :answer-field/id #uuid "5cc8d71a-f7ed-5fdf-86fe-f45189c1e899" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468777} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b7bdcb06-e317-5a3a-9e70-02fe6708ee55" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468114} {:answer/id #uuid "4beb574c-ecdc-5730-ab4c-de665302867c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468115}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468114} :answer-field/id #uuid "f99708f6-d8a6-5891-8014-c3ac976cd0cb" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468778} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e6d9a215-990f-586e-ad1c-3