-of-coordinates matrix from the basis $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\}$ to the basis $C=\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2},{c}_{3}\\}$ is given above. Find $[x]_{C}$ given that $x=4{b}_{2}-2{b}_{1}-3{b}_{3}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $x=4{b}_{2}-2{b}_{1}-3{b}_{3},$ we have\n\n$$\n[x]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n \n\nGiven the coordinates of $x$ relative to $B$ and the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C,$ we find the coordinates of $x$ relative to $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\,x\\,]_{C} & ={P}_{B\\to C}[\\,x\\,]_{B} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-7 \\\\ -14 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186440466 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5583d439-4b26-52b3-9794-1635eb018312" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440422} {:answer/id #uuid "5ed1a788-27da-548c-9bec-4712cdd0d589" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440423} {:answer/id #uuid "aa87788a-652c-5c09-96d7-b1ceb5b7f4ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440436} {:answer/id #uuid "cfd42ca8-7e84-5bc0-81bc-00e0d590afe7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440443} {:answer/id #uuid "de0299ce-78dd-576d-89cc-ca65aafc4c70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440448}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440448} :answer-field/id #uuid "33e79f79-0984-59ea-b9d7-5fe66d3a3c37" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440454}] :question/id #uuid "769b83ac-7384-56eb-8f7a-6aa51afc8a2a" :question/math-academy-id "q-113539" :question/problem "The change-of-coordinates matrix from the basis $B$ to the basis $C$ and the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B$ are given below. What is $[x]_{C}?$ \n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to C}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,[x]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Given the coordinates of $x$ relative to $B$ and the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C,$ we find the coordinates of $x$ relative to $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\,x\\,]_{C} & ={P}_{B\\to C}[\\,x\\,]_{B} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Coordinates of a Vector in a New Basis Given the Change-of-Coordinates Matrix"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124496 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124309 :question/id #uuid "a3911ca2-a357-5f37-8abc-e01e5518f24b" :question/math-academy-id "e-4840" :question/problem "The change-of-coordinates matrix from $\\mathcal{B}=\\{ \\mathbf{b}_1,\\mathbf{b}_2 \\}$ to $\\mathcal{C} = \\{ \\mathbf{c}_1,\\mathbf{c}_2 \\}$ is given below. Find $[\\mathbf{x}]_{\\mathcal{B}}$ given that $\\mathbf{x} =2\\mathbf{c}_1-6\\mathbf{c}_2.$\n\n![](images/15/15e0d0c04e0352356acab8001936031505931dac7eb7afefa1881dd333448e57.svg)" :question/worked-solution "We will use the change-of-coordinates formula in the form\n\n$$\n[\\,\\mathbf{x}\\,]_{\\mathcal{B}} = P_{\\small\\mathcal{C}\\to\\mathcal{B}} [\\,\\mathbf{x}\\,]_{\\mathcal{C}} .\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to find the change-of-coordinates matrix $P_{\\small\\mathcal{C}\\to\\mathcal{B}}$ from $\\mathcal{C}$ to $\\mathcal{B}.$ To do that, we compute the inverse of $P_{\\small\\mathcal{B}\\to\\mathcal{C}}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{C\\to B} & ={P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} \\\\  & ={\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 3 \\\\ 6 & -4\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(-4)(-4)-6\\cdot 3}\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -3 \\\\ -6 & -4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & \\frac{3}{2} \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that since $\\mathbf{x} = 2 \\mathbf{c}_1-6\\mathbf{c}_2,$ we obtain\n![](images/17/178769437e55f1822723ac4cc090efca62aac6be9e3ad9dc8f7971b8a6196484.svg)\n\nNow, we compute $[\\,\\mathbf{x}\\,]_{\\mathcal{B}}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\,x\\,]_{B} & ={P}_{C\\to B}[\\,x\\,]_{C} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & \\frac{3}{2} \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5ee52fd3-6c79-5016-ade5-46e7bfbb557a" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124994 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b3218afa-c5a1-5e45-b2a7-29995b720c79" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}12 \\\\ 27\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391999} {:answer/id #uuid "f25974c9-ca87-5bf9-957d-8b53cd37be8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392000} {:answer/id #uuid "48c64c3a-7f08-535f-a11d-91e574947824" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 22\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392001} {:answer/id #uuid "cf0a32bf-78a6-511f-9f75-0ac4d9b7caeb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}24 \\\\ 30\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392002} {:answer/id #uuid "81442015-4c62-5e1f-9ad1-d16a4137f7f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}22 \\\\ 35\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392003}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}22 \\\\ 35\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392003} :answer-field/id #uuid "fa84e0e3-e3ca-5864-9c75-6d5148345ac3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391998}] :question/id #uuid "f503090a-50ea-5c09-941f-e82b557a90db" :question/math-academy-id "q-36503" :question/problem "The change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C$ and the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $C$ are given below. What is $[x]_{B}?$ \n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to C}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,[x]_{C}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the change-of-coordinates formula in the form\n\n$$\n[\\,x\\,]_{B}={P}_{C\\to B}[\\,x\\,]_{C}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to find the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{C\\to B}$ from $C$ to $B.$ To do that, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to C}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{C\\to B} & ={P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} \\\\  & ={\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5\\cdot 2-(-3)\\cdot (-3)}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute $[\\,x\\,]_{B}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\,x\\,]_{B} & ={P}_{C\\to B}[\\,x\\,]_{C} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}22 \\\\ 35\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125034 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1aef89aa-352b-5bfd-b894-d5a6aa700de7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392059} {:answer/id #uuid "35c2dbc4-a502-58b1-b028-c6066cf70d56" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -\\frac{7}{2}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392060} {:answer/id #uuid "9cc2efdf-e18a-58d8-9ad6-5bdf0228a9fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -\\frac{7}{2}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392061} {:answer/id #uuid "7ccf6827-947c-53f9-9bbb-08f0c53653fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392062} {:answer/id #uuid "289737b2-0d6d-5390-9fae-aa676b2d8f39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392063}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392063} :answer-field/id #uuid "e30c4e35-75bd-5c3f-9c45-ae4bf9b81adc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392058}] :question/id #uuid "894b16d3-3e6a-5bd5-b6ff-86b2b95aa0cd" :question/math-academy-id "q-37154" :question/problem "The change-of-coordinates matrix from $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}$ to $C=\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\}$ is given below. Find $[x]_{B}$ given that $x=-3{c}_{1}-2{c}_{2}.$\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to C}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the change-of-coordinates formula in the form\n\n$$\n[\\,x\\,]_{B}={P}_{C\\to B}[\\,x\\,]_{C}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to find the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{C\\to B}$ from $C$ to $B.$ To do that, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to C}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{C\\to B} & ={P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} \\\\  & ={\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -4\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1\\cdot (-4)-(-2)\\cdot 3}\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ 1 & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that since $x=-3{c}_{1}-2{c}_{2},$ we obtain \n\n$$\n[x]_{C}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we compute $[\\,x\\,]_{B}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\,x\\,]_{B} & ={P}_{C\\to B}[\\,x\\,]_{C} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ 1 & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323807 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e412cca-3de6-5980-bb99-cf3bccf43fec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321257} {:answer/id #uuid "137c55e3-1ce7-52fa-871f-4778b481186a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321301} {:answer/id #uuid "930eac4b-99c1-548d-911a-4f0dbf0771a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322310} {:answer/id #uuid "9dd98043-a25b-5027-a9f0-593fb49217d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322391} {:answer/id #uuid "d2cab1f4-06ce-5d69-9f7d-a3f736d395e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322794}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322391} :answer-field/id #uuid "3e47d3d8-0d42-5d02-8f6a-ceceea2fa24c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323291}] :question/id #uuid "76994fe0-8052-50ba-9dfa-9fe567d9b172" :question/math-academy-id "q-36485" :question/problem "The change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C$ and the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $C$ are given below. What is $[x]_{B}?$ \n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to C}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -4\\end{bmatrix},\\,[x]_{C}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the change-of-coordinates formula in the form\n\n$$\n[\\,x\\,]_{B}={P}_{C\\to B}[\\,x\\,]_{C}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to find the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{C\\to B}$ from $C$ to $B.$ To do that, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to C}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{C\\to B} & ={P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} \\\\  & ={\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -4\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(-2)\\cdot (-4)-3\\cdot 3}\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -3 \\\\ -3 & -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute $[\\,x\\,]_{B}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\,x\\,]_{B} & ={P}_{C\\to B}[\\,x\\,]_{C} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351438 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6d08356c-7931-5cd9-9d11-4c39181be760" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349451} {:answer/id #uuid "9af31c0d-f620-5346-8cc8-0520d3750ee8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-9 \\\\ -8\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349828} {:answer/id #uuid "d7bf9bfb-32be-5f38-ad4d-61f15bcaba54" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350336} {:answer/id #uuid "e73a838e-f880-5ec9-8ca6-4f2bee27ab24" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350469} {:answer/id #uuid "f4ff9120-1464-5615-9c5e-ff1e12550f88" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350589}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349451} :answer-field/id #uuid "ddf5d9a8-e075-5599-8957-df3a4a61095c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351095}] :question/id #uuid "1a8774bf-f531-5684-a4ee-be071e1e5ed5" :question/math-academy-id "q-82599" :question/problem "The change-of-coordinates matrix from $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ to $C={{c}_{1},{c}_{2}}$ is given below. Find $[x]_{B}$ given that $x=3{c}_{1}-3{c}_{2}.$\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to C}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the change-of-coordinates formula in the form\n\n$$\n[\\,x\\,]_{B}={P}_{C\\to B}[\\,x\\,]_{C}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to find the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{C\\to B}$ from $C$ to $B.$ To do that, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to C}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{C\\to B} & ={P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} \\\\  & ={\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\cdot 3-(-1)\\cdot (-5)}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that since $x=3{c}_{1}-3{c}_{2},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n[x]_{C}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute $[\\,x\\,]_{B}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\,x\\,]_{B} & ={P}_{C\\to B}[\\,x\\,]_{C} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351452 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24a47585-dd72-5249-a458-79a5435b9a70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348762} {:answer/id #uuid "8138e059-eedd-5c90-9dc2-6259bf30ff25" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-7 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349635} {:answer/id #u