\\,x\\,]_{C} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & 5 \\\\ 5 & -4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-7 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186386696 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ef569771-c4e7-5291-a02a-eccb98516f64" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}16 \\\\ 42\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386698} {:answer/id #uuid "19f40148-c027-5e57-83ca-f9ce5e2e487f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ 13\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386699} {:answer/id #uuid "f2dbac90-d79d-5e74-a3e8-3e28846fd99d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386700} {:answer/id #uuid "8aadec7c-66e6-5275-836d-0b2d825fbd7b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}28 \\\\ 18\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386701} {:answer/id #uuid "54154bb7-e3f6-55f0-b690-aed92908791b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-16 \\\\ 26\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386702}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}28 \\\\ 18\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386701} :answer-field/id #uuid "30675a92-d5d0-5d0c-a77d-9c525c8b8db4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386697}] :question/id #uuid "6ed39867-0f3e-5f3d-ab65-536828c9ba67" :question/math-academy-id "q-113573" :question/problem "The change-of-coordinates matrix from $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}$ to $C=\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\}$ is given below. Find $[x]_{B}$ given that $x=2{c}_{1}-4{c}_{2}.$\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to C}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 \\\\ 5 & -8\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the change-of-coordinates formula in the form\n\n$$\n[\\,x\\,]_{B}={P}_{C\\to B}[\\,x\\,]_{C}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to find the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{C\\to B}$ from $C$ to $B.$ To do that, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to C}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{C\\to B} & ={P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} \\\\  & ={\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 \\\\ 5 & -8\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\cdot (-8)-(-3)\\cdot 5}\\begin{bmatrix}-8 & 3 \\\\ -5 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}8 & -3 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that since $x=2{c}_{1}-4{c}_{2},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n[x]_{C}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute $[\\,x\\,]_{B}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\,x\\,]_{B} & ={P}_{C\\to B}[\\,x\\,]_{C} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}8 & -3 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}28 \\\\ 18\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186394442 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "549a0eee-e056-5b3e-945c-dc08eab7d67e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394444} {:answer/id #uuid "780e5eeb-967c-58e6-9b97-e28954821893" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394445} {:answer/id #uuid "5fbfa154-65b9-54ed-a535-feab787fda53" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394446} {:answer/id #uuid "b9d33501-64aa-5fb9-b7f1-cd2d776eee3e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394447} {:answer/id #uuid "48d8e050-c67b-591d-a02d-6b6dede8752f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ -8\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394448}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394446} :answer-field/id #uuid "e2130ea6-8c98-546a-8865-99cd9a3a8e9c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394443}] :question/id #uuid "3a7ee4f4-73c6-5824-a327-bfe7ce4e304c" :question/math-academy-id "q-82707" :question/problem "The change-of-coordinates matrix from $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}$ to $C=\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\}$ is given below. Find $[x]_{B}$ given that $x=5{c}_{1}-{c}_{2}.$\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to C}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 10 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the change-of-coordinates formula in the form\n\n$$\n[\\,x\\,]_{B}={P}_{C\\to B}[\\,x\\,]_{C}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to find the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{C\\to B}$ from $C$ to $B.$ To do that, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to C}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{C\\to B} & ={P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} \\\\  & ={\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 10 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5\\cdot 5-2\\cdot 10}\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -10 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ -\\frac{2}{5} & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that since $x=5{c}_{1}-{c}_{2},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n[x]_{C}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute $[\\,x\\,]_{B}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\,x\\,]_{B} & ={P}_{C\\to B}[\\,x\\,]_{C} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ -\\frac{2}{5} & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186417185 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5c1b7743-c305-5999-a721-23098449b1cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417138} {:answer/id #uuid "76daf001-db03-5b02-b5ce-d1bdb4a9261e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417143} {:answer/id #uuid "848c95d9-4948-5e5b-b405-b76d8bb0404e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417146} {:answer/id #uuid "e45951f9-b2ac-5925-8dca-6a0e9e74ecc4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417167} {:answer/id #uuid "e5ad6413-b74c-561a-9d52-2593718ee8e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-7 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417168}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417167} :answer-field/id #uuid "259091c3-ae0d-594d-b51a-a8e034136037" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417174}] :question/id #uuid "2be7f5e5-3b31-5fb7-85df-a4fc0339bd35" :question/math-academy-id "q-82598" :question/problem "The change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C$ and the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $C$ are given below. What is $[x]_{B}?$ \n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to C}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -4\\end{bmatrix},\\,[x]_{C}=\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the change-of-coordinates formula in the form\n\n$$\n[\\,x\\,]_{B}={P}_{C\\to B}[\\,x\\,]_{C}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to find the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{C\\to B}$ from $C$ to $B.$ To do that, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to C}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{C\\to B} & ={P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} \\\\  & ={\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -4\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(-2)\\cdot (-4)-3\\cdot 2}\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -2 \\\\ -3 & -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -1 \\\\ -\\frac{3}{2} & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute $[\\,x\\,]_{B}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\,x\\,]_{B} & ={P}_{C\\to B}[\\,x\\,]_{C} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -1 \\\\ -\\frac{3}{2} & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186417192 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a297d16-52a8-53eb-9dad-1a87b66f4056" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417128} {:answer/id #uuid "67ef9947-0abd-58ce-bfaa-502e27646e6a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417141} {:answer/id #uuid "86daf74f-004a-52d1-918a-94714d07c50d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417148} {:answer/id #uuid "87c5730a-1432-52b5-aaf3-ec874082be11" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417149} {:answer/id #uuid "ed545a0d-bb95-5b28-bd97-fb2a46aed464" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417169}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417169} :answer-field/id #uuid "5d503694-4c65-5f5e-80a7-c8e1b24fe6d1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417177}] :question/id #uuid "f0cfdcd8-92d0-5768-aa59-2dc769427d08" :question/math-academy-id "q-113597" :question/problem "The change-of-coordinates matrix from $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ to $C={{c}_{1},{c}_{2}}$ is given below. Find $[x]_{B}$ given that $x=4{c}_{1}+6{c}_{2}.$ \n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to C}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 7 \\\\ 3 & 6\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the change-of-coordinates formula in the form\n\n$$\n[\\,x\\,]_{B}={P}_{C\\to B}[\\,x\\,]_{C}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to find the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{C\\to B}$ from $C$ to $B.$ To do that, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to C}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{C\\to B} & ={P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} \\\\  & ={\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 7 \\\\ 3 & 6\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4\\cdot 6-7\\cdot 3}\\begin{bmatrix}6 & -7 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -\\frac{7}{3} \\\\ -1 & \\frac{4}{3}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that since $x=4{c}_{1}+6{c}_{2},$ we obtain  \n\n$$\n[x]_{C}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we compute $[\\,x\\,]_{B}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\,x\\,]_{B} & ={P}_{C\\to B}[\\,x\\,]_{C} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -\\frac{7}{3} \\\\ -1 & \\frac{4}{3}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186440464 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05a2a04d-6fe7-5a0d-8718-80558dc272b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -13\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440398} {:answer/id #uuid "4b07ccd2-15b5-5fe4-9051-5d908e60ebd4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -8\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440417} {:answer/id #uuid "50b3b88a-a623-50e5-b968-d9227a27e597" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}18 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440420} {:answer/id #uuid "c51f010d-b055-55be-a901-8dda67213b6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440438} {:answer/id #uuid "cfa60034-0dcd-5f83-8b52-44d789dd2759" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440442}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -13\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440398} :answer-field/id #uuid "ca6335cf-a241-5413-8b14-741fb6ccabc6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440460}] :question/id #uuid "50a9b032-ab11-5594-a8b4-f98e14bf6ea6" :question/math-academy-id "q-82706" :question/problem "The change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C$ and the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $C$ are given below. What is $[x]_{B}?$ \n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to C}=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 4 \\\\ 12 & 7\\end{bmatrix},\\,[x]_{C}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the change-of-coordinates formula in the form\n\n$$\n[\\,x\\,]_{B}={P}_{C\\to B}[\\,x\\,]_{C}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to find the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{C\\to B}$ from $C$ to $B.$ To do that, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to C}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{C\\to B} & ={P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} \\\\  & ={\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 4 \\\\ 12 & 7\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7\\cdot 7-12\\cdot 4}\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -4 \\\\ -12 & 7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -4 \\\\ -12 & 7\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute $[\\,x\\,]_{B}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\,x\\,]_{B} & ={P}_{C\\to B}[\\,x\\,]_{C} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -4 \\\\ -12 & 7\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -13\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186440465 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07df0399-5b7b-513e-bfe4-682fc2093392" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440399} {:answer/id #uuid "1f5c1c5a-e4ea-5d65-95cb-9752b676bf64" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440407} {:answer/id #uuid "c77af8ac-86cc-50b1-9ef0-e91ba1f365af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440439} {:answer/id #uuid "f07972b5-b529-5e8a-8ee6-b20071370ee9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440449} {:answer/id #uuid "fb09d36c-bb40-569c-94ed-c0a08e942a34" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440450}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440450} :answer-field/id #uuid "db389e57-4899-5138-b87d-2318a36bc5bc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440461}] :question/id #uuid "7107964a-37f7-5d19-a3ab-82f544f38d24" :question/math-academy-id "q-113593" :question/problem "The change-of-coordinates matrix from $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}$ to $C=\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\}$ is given below. Find $[x]_{B}$ given that $x=2{c}_{1}-2{c}_{2}.$\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to C}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -4 \\\\ -5 & 6\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the change-of-coordinates formula in the form\n\n$$\n[\\,x\\,]_{B}={P}_{C\\to B}[\\,x\\,]_{C}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to find the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{C\\to B}$ from $C$ to $B.$ To do that, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to C}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{C\\to B} & ={P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} \\\\  & ={\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -4 \\\\ -5 & 6\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3\\cdot 6-(-4)\\cdot (-5)}\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 4 \\\\ 5 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -2 \\\\ -\\frac{5}{2} & -\\frac{3}{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that since $x=2{c}_{1}-2{c}_{2},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n[x]_{C}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute $[\\,x\\,]_{B}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\,x\\,]_{B} & ={P}_{C\\to B}[\\,x\\,]_{C} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -2 \\\\ -\\frac{5}{2} & -\\frac{3}{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186440469 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3aa4bb15-cd67-5f6e-b5ce-1a199a6dd8a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440411} {:answer/id #uuid "45687a63-f60a-5bfb-a261-9e94c6a4c076" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ -10\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440414} {:answer/id #uuid "796a9b6a-3558-5233-a3ac-8460d1cea27f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440428} {:answer/id #uuid "cb21b0ff-7e60-5f91-938c-d9d9d7cbf7a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -10\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440440} {:answer/id #uuid "cc371831-0ddf-5330-a6c1-805660c3647a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440441}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ -10\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440414} :answer-field/id #uuid "549d99dc-683d-5071-97ad-668e834f5eb6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440456}] :question/id #uuid "9bc30c67-14a3-514e-87f9-9c3583feaf85" :question/math-academy-id "q-82601" :question/problem "The change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C$ and the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $C$ are given below. What is $[x]_{B}?$ \n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to C}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,[x]_{C}=\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the change-of-coordinates formula in the form\n\n$$\n[\\,x\\,]_{B}={P}_{C\\to B}[\\,x\\,]_{C}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to find the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{C\\to B}$ from $C$ to $B.$ To do that, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to C}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{C\\to B} & ={P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} \\\\  & ={\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3\\cdot 3-4\\cdot 2}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute $[\\,x\\,]_{B}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\,x\\,]_{B} & ={P}_{C\\to B}[\\,x\\,]_{C} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ -10\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186486427 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1696c49c-b8ba-5c9f-a1e2-a234d7a12381" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485804} {:answer/id #uuid "33eeaaae-80c9-51a7-944e-f618a820b3bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485862} {:answer/id #uuid "35031deb-a4ba-5495-89d6-18fe7aca9f79" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485864} {:answer/id #uuid "bb2528e3-8cd1-5c53-9f19-daeb351a37d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486101} {:answer/id #uuid "e673df76-6d49-52f2-85e7-cffc12218f67" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486189}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486101} :answer-field/id #uuid "d0731c0a-4746-54da-b38a-46b9b2e964b1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486320}] :question/id #uuid "ae7fdbe5-ac31-5cc5-8e79-33235643a822" :question/math-academy-id "q-36502" :question/problem "The change-of-coordinates matrix from $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}$ to $C=\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\}$ is given below. Find $[x]_{B}$ given that $x={c}_{1}+4{c}_{2}.$\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to C}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ 6 & 10\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the change-of-coordinates formula in the form\n\n$$\n[\\,x\\,]_{B}={P}_{C\\to B}[\\,x\\,]_{C}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to find the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{C\\to B}$ from $C$ to $B.$ To do that, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to C}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{C\\to B} & ={P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} \\\\  & ={\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ 6 & 10\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\cdot 10-6\\cdot 3}\\begin{bmatrix}10 & -3 \\\\ -6 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that since $x={c}_{1}+4{c}_{2},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n[x]_{C}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute $[\\,x\\,]_{B}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\,x\\,]_{B} & ={P}_{C\\to B}[\\,x\\,]_{C} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186486444 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15690e8b-c556-578a-a848-9e2012319066" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485801} {:answer/id #uuid "2ce04a03-a227-57a9-bb1f-9d7b6996fb5a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485848} {:answer/id #uuid "972d0aed-9872-5a09-9680-0c04b590dfee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486037} {:answer/id #uuid "b85661ff-f141-5e76-a9a5-e29f75d6b6b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486097} {:answer/id #uuid "d2bcf6bc-21ea-5ab1-b19b-a0bda85a2f8c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486151}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486097} :answer-field/id #uuid "f917e741-700b-51ed-9e8c-db10a05c79b2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486345}] :question/id #uuid "cd3d1f8f-1ec9-5277-bd94-fc774bb919de" :question/math-academy-id "q-113595" :question/problem "The change-of-coordinates matrix from $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}$ to $C=\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\}$ is given below. Find $[x]_{B}$ given that $x=2{c}_{1}-{c}_{2}.$\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to C}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the change-of-coordinates formula in the form\n\n$$\n[\\,x\\,]_{B}={P}_{C\\to B}[\\,x\\,]_{C}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to find the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{C\\to B}$ from $C$ to $B.$ To do that, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to C}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{C\\to B} & ={P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} \\\\  & ={\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4\\cdot 5-5\\cdot 3}\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -5 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ -\\frac{3}{5} & \\frac{4}{5}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that since $x=2{c}_{1}-{c}_{2},$ we obtain \n\n$$\n[x]_{C}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we compute $[\\,x\\,]_{B}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\,x\\,]_{B} & ={P}_{C\\to B}[\\,x\\,]_{C} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ -\\frac{3}{5} & \\frac{4}{5}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Coordinates of a Vector in a New Basis Given the Inverse Change-of-Coordinates Matrix"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124497 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124310 :question/id #uuid "a2d3629f-5b7c-5b65-998f-8754ff11e7b7" :question/math-academy-id "e-4841" :question/problem "The basis $\\mathcal{B}$ of $\\mathbb{R}^2$ and the coordinates of the vector $\\mathbf{x}$ relative to the standard basis $\\mathcal{S}$ are given below. Find $[\\mathbf{x}]_{\\mathcal{B}}.$\n\n![](images/0b/0b395052cc098a6daeb50037d07223b20fb93163c10c31a432c7fb9c9a7804db.svg)" :question/worked-solution "We will use the change-of-coordinates formula in the form\n\n$$\n[\\,\\mathbf{x}\\,]_{\\mathcal{B}} = P_{\\small\\mathcal{S}\\to\\mathcal{B}} [\\,\\mathbf{x}\\,]_{\\mathcal{S}} .\n$$\n\nFirst, recall that the change-of-coordinates matrix from $\\mathcal{B}$ to $\\mathcal{S}$ is the matrix whose columns are the vectors of $\\mathcal{B}$ relative to the standard basis $\\mathcal{S}.$ As a result, we have\n\n![](images/82/82e477164a2708a6f8e7f1142dce3e290d3aa216b5828e0523c16555533f02b7.svg)\n\nNow, we need to find the change-of-coordinates matrix $P_{\\small\\mathcal{S}\\to\\mathcal{B}}$ from $\\mathcal{S}$ to $\\mathcal{B}.$ To do that, we compute the inverse of $P_{\\small\\mathcal{B}\\to\\mathcal{S}}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{S\\to B} & ={P}_{B\\to S}^{-1} \\\\  & ={\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 10\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1\\cdot 10-3\\cdot 3}\\begin{bmatrix}10 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}10 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute $[\\,\\mathbf{x}\\,]_{\\mathcal{B}}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\,x\\,]_{B} & ={P}_{S\\to B}[\\,x\\,]_{S} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}10 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7f58bd46-07f7-54a5-8499-5e4e3515b610" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124993 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1dcd4ef1-4949-58ef-aa67-9540954fdc1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321374} {:answer/id #uuid "41ecfd30-c58f-5e8b-8238-dbc9493bac67" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321670} {:answer/id #uuid "46420e90-1c10-5b3a-a995-8806f1bcee0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321702} {:answer/id #uuid "6e560467-13af-562b-ad43-d89f3b3f3260" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322002} {:answer/id #uuid "d1bf20ff-37e7-5af1-a632-1f6b46091107" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322785}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321702} :answer-field/id #uuid "4370689f-d468-5230-a5de-f45535b13a11" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323298}] :question/id #uuid "9b5f682f-a0de-52f6-930d-b54c3a22eede" :question/math-academy-id "q-36488" :question/problem "$$\nB={\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ -8\\end{bmatrix}},\\,[x]_{S}=\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe basis $B$ of ${R}^{2}$ and the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the standard basis $S$ are given above. Find $[x]_{B}.$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the change-of-coordinates formula in the form\n\n$$\n[\\,x\\,]_{B}={P}_{S\\to B}[\\,x\\,]_{S}.\n$$\n\nFirst, recall that the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $S$ is the matrix whose columns are the vectors of $B$ relative to the standard basis $S.$ As a result, we have\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to S}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 9 \\\\ -2 & -8\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{S\\to B}$ from $S$ to $B.$ To do that, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to S}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{S\\to B} & ={P}_{B\\to S}^{-1} \\\\  & ={\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 9 \\\\ -2 & -8\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3\\cdot (-8)-9\\cdot (-2)}\\begin{bmatrix}-8 & -9 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{4}{3} & \\frac{3}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{3} & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute $[\\,x\\,]_{B}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\,x\\,]_{B} & ={P}_{S\\to B}[\\,x\\,]_{S} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{4}{3} & \\frac{3}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{3} & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125036 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7b3fc777-c87e-5494-9361-753fc99b8a92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417145} {:answer/id #uuid "af2e1656-5790-518b-ae95-17ddec42b6bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417157} {:answer/id #uuid "c820d187-6507-5a27-8119-ca85d381bd74" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417165} {:answer/id #uuid "d1949552-5c2a-51ed-85be-630d9f8df6a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417166} {:answer/id #uuid "fc368894-a420-5e78-a8ce-445dfc038e7c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417173}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417166} :answer-field/id #uuid "77968fba-758e-5c47-b717-abe8d60fbc59" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417179}] :question/id #uuid "618e1711-d591-5872-b815-9d14ad33b674" :question/math-academy-id "q-37160" :question/problem "$$\nB=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 16\\end{bmatrix}\\},\\,[x]_{S}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe basis $B$ of ${R}^{2}$ and the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the standard basis $S$ are given above. Find $[x]_{B}.$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the change-of-coordinates formula in the form\n\n$$\n[\\,x\\,]_{B}={P}_{S\\to B}[\\,x\\,]_{S}.\n$$\n\nFirst, recall that the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $S$ is the matrix whose columns are the vectors of $B$ relative to the standard basis $S.$ As a result, we have\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to S}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 16\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{S\\to B}$ from $S$ to $B.$ To do that, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to S}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{S\\to B} & ={P}_{B\\to S}^{-1} \\\\  & ={\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 16\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1\\cdot 16-3\\cdot 5}\\begin{bmatrix}16 & -5 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}16 & -5 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute $[\\,x\\,]_{B}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\,x\\,]_{B} & ={P}_{S\\to B}[\\,x\\,]_{S} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}16 & -5 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247377 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0111ba18-14c2-5781-8010-722128c79697" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244318} {:answer/id #uuid "a2007ea3-9bcf-5eb2-a398-3c3026f0d19c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}15 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245758} {:answer/id #uuid "c07f9713-d7ef-5785-83bf-b5366930e083" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246028} {:answer/id #uuid "e0a82ad7-4173-547d-870b-3097212ee0d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246315} {:answer/id #uuid "e0df6a1b-3e14-561b-bae5-b111612833c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246317}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246315} :answer-field/id #uuid "a5f06954-e77b-50c5-b48b-ad2eea059c5b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246844}] :question/id #uuid "ca416b56-0c6d-5fb5-8b76-d2124cfd2e38" :question/math-academy-id "q-113600" :question/problem "$$\nB={\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}},\\,[x]_{S}=\\begin{bmatrix}15 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe basis $B$ of ${R}^{2}$ and the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the standard basis $S$ are given above. Find $[x]_{B}.$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the change-of-coordinates formula in the form\n\n$$\n[\\,x\\,]_{B}={P}_{S\\to B}[\\,x\\,]_{S}.\n$$\n\nFirst, recall that the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $S$ is the matrix whose columns are the vectors of $B$ relative to the standard basis $S.$ As a result, we have\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to S}=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{S\\to B}$ from $S$ to $B.$ To do that, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to S}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{S\\to B} & ={P}_{B\\to S}^{-1} \\\\  & ={\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 3\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6\\cdot 3-3\\cdot 5}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -3 \\\\ -5 & 6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ -\\frac{5}{3} & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute $[\\,x\\,]_{B}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\,x\\,]_{B} & ={P}_{S\\to B}[\\,x\\,]_{S} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ -\\frac{5}{3} & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}15 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247379 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05662116-9ed5-51f3-a508-b1ed64f2e349" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244359} {:answer/id #uuid "33a9596f-e4e0-5e92-b079-84b8cbdda157" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ -11\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244776} {:answer/id #uuid "7294001d-9a70-5e64-8833-bfc2b3f3c0db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}25 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245337} {:answer/id #uuid "b6b79f00-6365-55a2-9673-e57f0f1960c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}16 \\\\ 21\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245947} {:answer/id #uuid "f5b08e24-4041-566d-9201-1f4cbd15de31" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}19 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246483}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244359} :answer-field/id #uuid "12b31fac-75a2-50ec-9978-bbb512fe8ff1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246582}] :question/id #uuid "162a4f62-2177-5623-998d-5746dbddde07" :question/math-academy-id "q-113606" :question/problem "$$\nB=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}-7 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}\\},\\,[x]_{S}=\\begin{bmatrix}18 \\\\ -9\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe basis $B$ of ${R}^{2}$ and the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the standard basis $S$ are given above. Find $[x]_{B}.$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the change-of-coordinates formula in the form\n\n$$\n[\\,x\\,]_{B}={P}_{S\\to B}[\\,x\\,]_{S}.\n$$\n\nFirst, recall that the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $S$ is the matrix whose columns are the vectors of $B$ relative to the standard basis $S.$ As a result, we have\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to S}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -7 \\\\ -3 & 6\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{S\\to B}$ from $S$ to $B.$ To do that, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to S}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{S\\to B} & ={P}_{B\\to S}^{-1} \\\\  & ={\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -7 \\\\ -3 & 6\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5\\cdot 6-(-7)\\cdot (-3)}\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 7 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{7}{9} \\\\ \\frac{1}{3} & \\frac{5}{9}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute $[\\,x\\,]_{B}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\,x\\,]_{B} & ={P}_{S\\to B}[\\,x\\,]_{S} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{7}{9} \\\\ \\frac{1}{3} & \\frac{5}{9}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}18 \\\\ -9\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351453 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "037e3267-6d37-527e-807c-7afdb1a65ab2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348480} {:answer/id #uuid "1248c56a-747b-5f04-a4be-55be8f0f2299" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348605} {:answer/id #uuid "28d1ae32-20d0-5a3a-b2db-04a064ab2833" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-7 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348797} {:answer/id #uuid "568c3ed7-20a6-598e-b279-602ee3204b62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349238} {:answer/id #uuid "b6813564-4311-50aa-9c0d-ea63994c4573" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350060}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350060} :answer-field/id #uuid "1df097c5-29e4-5371-a601-2fadd4a36869" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350762}] :question/id #uuid "5ee6ca5a-3bdd-5fec-a9fa-7000d4a0cb6f" :question/math-academy-id "q-82710" :question/problem "$$\nB={\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 11\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}},\\,[x]_{S}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe basis $B$ of ${R}^{2}$ and the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the standard basis $S$ are given above. Find $[x]_{B}.$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the change-of-coordinates formula in the form\n\n$$\n[\\,x\\,]_{B}={P}_{S\\to B}[\\,x\\,]_{S}.\n$$\n\nFirst, recall that the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $S$ is the matrix whose columns are the vectors of $B$ relative to the standard basis $S.$ As a result, we have\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to S}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 1 \\\\ 11 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{S\\to B}$ from $S$ to $B.$ To do that, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to S}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{S\\to B} & ={P}_{B\\to S}^{-1} \\\\  & ={\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 1 \\\\ 11 & 3\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4\\cdot 3-11\\cdot 1}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ -11 & 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ -11 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute $[\\,x\\,]_{B}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\,x\\,]_{B} & ={P}_{S\\to B}[\\,x\\,]_{S} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ -11 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186394414 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9b1e14eb-c6fe-5d5e-a0dc-b061059559c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394416} {:answer/id #uuid "985b430f-4b57-5849-b48f-23adc660de97" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394417} {:answer/id #uuid "dab5b566-c168-514d-b3c6-1c83c5b47cd0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394418} {:answer/id #uuid "a6a4ab04-a137-58d3-a387-4f383d0ae878" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394419} {:answer/id #uuid "71cfe1b4-e7cb-5edf-9ce0-5c9a0fe890fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394420}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394417} :answer-field/id #uuid "e7cbaef8-14a8-5424-bff9-cdd4ca81b618" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394415}] :question/id #uuid "5c7d63da-59ab-5308-9b89-bf650fb9db9b" :question/math-academy-id "q-82606" :question/problem "$$\nB=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\\},\\,[x]_{S}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe basis $B$ of ${R}^{2}$ and the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the standard basis $S$ are given above. Find $[x]_{B}.$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the change-of-coordinates formula in the form\n\n$$\n[\\,x\\,]_{B}={P}_{S\\to B}[\\,x\\,]_{S}.\n$$\n\nFirst, recall that the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $S$ is the matrix whose columns are the vectors of $B$ relative to the standard basis $S.$ As a result, we have\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to S}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 9 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{S\\to B}$ from $S$ to $B.$ To do that, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to S}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{S\\to B} & ={P}_{B\\to S}^{-1} \\\\  & ={\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 9 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5\\cdot 2-1\\cdot 9}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -9 \\\\ -1 & 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -9 \\\\ -1 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute $[\\,x\\,]_{B}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\,x\\,]_{B} & ={P}_{S\\to B}[\\,x\\,]_{S} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -9 \\\\ -1 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186394421 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "84bf4f13-8394-5e74-8611-52bcbe63b443" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394423} {:answer/id #uuid "a4f43405-b85b-5f16-ae6f-5e4abfc15221" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394424} {:answer/id #uuid "1be8e3f6-f794-5e2a-9dc7-026e640b732f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}12 \\\\ -17\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394425} {:answer/id #uuid "924d16bd-723c-52e2-9669-dce0fa52dce9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-10 \\\\ -18\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394426} {:answer/id #uuid "80c96893-628f-5b23-b717-b15529348c04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394427}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-10 \\\\ -18\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394426} :answer-field/id #uuid "4dc08976-f574-52b6-a28f-57c50285b1e0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394422}] :question/id #uuid "13aef9df-8682-5fe0-a906-e0817933e236" :question/math-academy-id "q-82609" :question/problem "$$\nB=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\},\\,[x]_{S}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe basis $B$ of ${R}^{2}$ and the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the standard basis $S$ are given above. Find $[x]_{B}.$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the change-of-coordinates formula in the form\n\n$$\n[\\,x\\,]_{B}={P}_{S\\to B}[\\,x\\,]_{S}.\n$$\n\nFirst, recall that the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $S$ is the matrix whose columns are the vectors of $B$ relative to the standard basis $S.$ As a result, we have\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to S}=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -4 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{S\\to B}$ from $S$ to $B.$ To do that, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to S}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{S\\to B} & ={P}_{B\\to S}^{-1} \\\\  & ={\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -4 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7\\cdot 1-(-2)\\cdot (-4)}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -4 \\\\ -2 & -7\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute $[\\,x\\,]_{B}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\,x\\,]_{B} & ={P}_{S\\to B}[\\,x\\,]_{S} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -4 \\\\ -2 & -7\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-10 \\\\ -18\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186417184 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "339eb9d7-c3ff-5722-b2a4-62c01e506dfe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417130} {:answer/id #uuid "7545326f-2ed3-5b45-b83f-fdce64ffd43b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417142} {:answer/id #uuid "c0ab3da6-d52a-52fe-8824-525245387581" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417162} {:answer/id #uuid "f99a0a3e-8e69-5c5a-8d55-fb74464b4d49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417171} {:answer/id #uuid "fa770ac4-af40-5a3c-b0e8-fb5ff74934d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417172}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417172} :answer-field/id #uuid "61a8f832-f2b3-5123-8233-870da3bb21e1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417178}] :question/id #uuid "15cdd9a6-5092-51ed-93a5-b2dd11d2ff12" :question/math-academy-id "q-82713" :question/problem "$$\nB=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\\},\\,[x]_{S}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe basis $B$ of ${R}^{2}$ and the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the standard basis $S$ are given above. Find $[x]_{B}.$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the change-of-coordinates formula in the form\n\n$$\n[\\,x\\,]_{B}={P}_{S\\to B}[\\,x\\,]_{S}.\n$$\n\nFirst, recall that the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $S$ is the matrix whose columns are the vectors of $B$ relative to the standard basis $S.$ As a result, we have\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to S}=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{S\\to B}$ from $S$ to $B.$ To do that, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to S}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{S\\to B} & ={P}_{B\\to S}^{-1} \\\\  & ={\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7\\cdot 2-3\\cdot 5}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -5 \\\\ -3 & 7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 5 \\\\ 3 & -7\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute $[\\,x\\,]_{B}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\,x\\,]_{B} & ={P}_{S\\to B}[\\,x\\,]_{S} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 5 \\\\ 3 & -7\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436248 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "426822c2-147e-581d-8735-96a3bffe8321" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-12 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436236} {:answer/id #uuid "5c39bc95-ae02-5c17-9a57-15db094b94c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436238} {:answer/id #uuid "89f6cf40-819f-5c6b-aeaf-667b443a0b60" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 11\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436240} {:answer/id #uuid "e55ca324-fff5-5f74-ad7a-3c6af6f7f1cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}36 \\\\ 13\\end{bma