e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450649}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450649} :answer-field/id #uuid "623efc55-bdf4-53da-9936-ec2df1772b9d" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451278} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e7ca6a7b-d2c1-579c-8b4e-c3fc51e76679" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450650} {:answer/id #uuid "460bc98c-aa4d-5008-abd2-b4b13e84f625" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450651}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450650} :answer-field/id #uuid "5059dfed-f97b-5c68-860f-943b60870dcb" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451279} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20fd12d0-0b82-5d63-b678-fdb08097e4e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450652} {:answer/id #uuid "dd3ba80b-43c0-5469-926f-886110b94004" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450653}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450652} :answer-field/id #uuid "d414d56d-e135-5893-a7d7-26e4a83fd3f2" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451280}] :question/id #uuid "628bddc5-7db2-5c2d-bca2-c9a2f11c4f87" :question/math-academy-id "q-42381" :question/problem "$$\nO=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix},\\,P=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 5 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,R=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the matrices $O,P,$ and $R?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The product $OP$ is well defined\n\n- **II.** The product $OR$ is well defined\n\n- **III.** The product $PR$ is well defined" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $O$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix, $P$ is a $2\\times 3$ matrix, and $R$ is a $1\\times 3$ row vector.\n\nThere are $2$ columns in $O$ and $2$ rows in $P.$ Since the number of columns in $O$ equals the number of rows in $P,$ the matrices $O$ and $P$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{O}_{3\\times \\boxed{\\text{2}}}{\\times }_{✓}{P}_{\\boxed{\\text{2}}\\times 3}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there are $2$ columns in $O$ and $1$ rows in $R.$ Since the number of columns in $O$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $R,$ the matrices $O$ and $R$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{O}_{3\\times 2}{\\times }_{\\ne }{R}_{1\\times 3}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nFinally, there are $3$ columns in $P$ and $1$ rows in $R.$ Since the number of columns in $P$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $R,$ the matrices $P$ and $R$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{P}_{2\\times 3}{\\times }_{\\ne }{R}_{1\\times 3}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nTherefore, statement I is true, while statements II and III are false."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562871 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "076c6b2a-e1d0-5505-b700-bcf004ce4d75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562854} {:answer/id #uuid "cc7f3c0d-6cd0-5f80-8b00-c608989978ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562907}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562854} :answer-field/id #uuid "1073773b-df59-5220-8043-a441e8a3b974" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562856} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8fc9c401-1e65-5873-89b4-5ede83dca30d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562888} {:answer/id #uuid "fd7fd980-eed2-51e5-9c91-bb2c4b24efb7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562921}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562921} :answer-field/id #uuid "a1b98f72-cdd0-540c-895f-00b0413680c5" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562894} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4607e018-576d-516c-bd98-9f6231ff371d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562867} {:answer/id #uuid "5e879290-41ce-5caa-9a80-54fb5adc6df8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562875}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562875} :answer-field/id #uuid "cbcce078-a3f1-5646-afef-3c0d9a54a619" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562906}] :question/id #uuid "514aa297-d018-5213-8e1d-3b49622a8fe3" :question/problem "$$\nO=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -3 & -5 & -5\\end{bmatrix},\\,P=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,R=\\begin{bmatrix}-8 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 6 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 7 & 6 \\\\ 4 & -7 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the matrices $O,P,$ and $R?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The product $OP$ is well defined\n\n- **II.** The product $PR$ is well defined\n\n- **III.** The product $PO$ is well defined" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $O$ is a $1\\times 4$ row vector, $P$ is a $5\\times 1$ column vector, and $R$ is a $5\\times 3$ matrix.\n\nThere are $4$ columns in $O$ and $5$ rows in $P.$ Since the number of columns in $O$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $P,$ the matrices $O$ and $P$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{O}_{1\\times 4}{\\times }_{\\ne }{P}_{5\\times 1}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there is $1$ column in $P$ and $5$ rows in $R.$ Since the number of columns in $P$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $R,$ the matrices $P$ and $R$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{P}_{5\\times 1}{\\times }_{\\ne }{R}_{5\\times 3}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nFinally, there is $1$ column in $P$ and $1$ row in $O.$ Since the number of columns in $P$ equals the number of rows in $O,$ the matrices $P$ and $O$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{P}_{5\\times \\boxed{\\text{1}}}{\\times }_{✓}{O}_{\\boxed{\\text{1}}\\times 4}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nTherefore, statement III is true, while statements I and II are false."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562872 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7f4356be-29f1-5e2b-830b-308a53df5c34" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562882} {:answer/id #uuid "85c9a81f-67cf-5cc7-90ed-a7b1dbdd973d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562885}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562882} :answer-field/id #uuid "63b06bda-1c4c-596d-b2b7-2455e8bb3e84" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562878} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4c2fb6f9-03f7-5731-ba5a-e3e4edd662b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562868} {:answer/id #uuid "4d370fc6-4fed-5c27-900c-ba8012cedd47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562869}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562869} :answer-field/id #uuid "b42c3153-374b-54ee-86c7-d7414ae8c1d5" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562899} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "934a6aee-e168-56ff-aaa0-3c4a7d248df1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562890} {:answer/id #uuid "db1d43c6-c9b4-5900-96b1-0aa4ef8e6ae3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562912}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562890} :answer-field/id #uuid "fb318e8d-7c03-55c8-bc35-aa74f911f214" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562920}] :question/id #uuid "55f9a3f4-1446-576a-9dd6-8f5cec99c326" :question/problem "$$\nO=\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,P=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -2\\end{bmatrix},\\,R=\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & -4 \\\\ -1 & -7 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -4 \\\\ 4 & 8\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the matrices $O,P,$ and $R?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The product $OR$ is well defined\n\n- **II.** The product $PO$ is well defined\n\n- **III.** The product $OP$ is well defined" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $O$ is a $3\\times 1$ column vector, $P$ is a $1\\times 2$ row vector, and $R$ is a $5\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nThere is $1$ column in $O$ and $5$ rows in $R.$ Since the number of columns in $O$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $R,$ the matrices $O$ and $R$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{O}_{3\\times 1}{\\times }_{\\ne }{R}_{5\\times 2}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there are $2$ columns in $P$ and $3$ rows in $O.$ Since the number of columns in $P$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $O,$ the matrices $P$ and $O$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{P}_{1\\times 2}{\\times }_{\\ne }{O}_{3\\times 1}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nFinally, there is $1$ column in $O$ and $1$ row in $P.$ Since the number of columns in $O$ equals the number of rows in $P,$ the matrices $O$ and $P$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{O}_{3\\times \\boxed{\\text{1}}}{\\times }_{✓}{P}_{\\boxed{\\text{1}}\\times 2}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nTherefore, statement III is true, while statements I and II are false."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562881 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34dafa4d-3944-582e-bbf7-64a2dcc62647" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562862} {:answer/id #uuid "d55b794e-24e2-5354-bfec-ef76085b2a8c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562909}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562909} :answer-field/id #uuid "3045f8ab-525f-5485-b581-68eae6f98ef3" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562860} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34e4c5ce-7e9c-5530-8b6b-ec090d2ebab0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562863} {:answer/id #uuid "a87f780f-4b8f-5015-b434-03be4bcc01d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562896}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562863} :answer-field/id #uuid "45d02062-6090-52e6-a662-c6361863dc12" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562865} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a4cd583-5b45-56dc-a6e1-195b989eb2a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562858} {:answer/id #uuid "63547524-da22-5745-afb6-a330347919c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562877}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562858} :answer-field/id #uuid "8307eb05-c0ad-51ff-8381-69c2aa369a62" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562884}] :question/id #uuid "795f6284-9977-53c9-b26a-515ee6438422" :question/problem "$$\nO=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -6 & -9 & -1 & 4 \\\\ -9 & 4 & 2 & 8 & 4 \\\\ 6 & 8 & 4 & -4 & -8 \\\\ -1 & 9 & -3 & -7 & 5\\end{bmatrix},\\,P=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & -5 & -2\\end{bmatrix},\\,R=\\begin{bmatrix}-9 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the matrices $O,P,$ and $R?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The product $RO$ is well defined\n\n- **II.** The product $PR$ is well defined\n\n- **III.** The product $RP$ is well defined" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $O$ is a $4\\times 5$ matrix, $P$ is a $1\\times 4$ row vector, and $R$ is a $2\\times 1$ column vector.\n\nThere is $1$ column in $R$ and $4$ rows in $O.$ Since the number of columns in $R$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $O,$ the matrices $R$ and $O$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{R}_{2\\times 1}{\\times }_{\\ne }{O}_{4\\times 5}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there are $4$ columns in $P$ and $2$ rows in $R.$ Since the number of columns in $P$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $R,$ the matrices $P$ and $R$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{P}_{1\\times 4}{\\times }_{\\ne }{R}_{2\\times 1}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nFinally, there is $1$ column in $R$ and $1$ row in $P.$ Since the number of columns in $R$ equals the number of rows in $P,$ the matrices $R$ and $P$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{R}_{2\\times \\boxed{\\text{1}}}{\\times }_{✓}{P}_{\\boxed{\\text{1}}\\times 4}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nTherefore, statement III is true, while statements I and II are false."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562887 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02a6580c-0d89-558b-b971-11e565184416" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562853} {:answer/id #uuid "32a9097c-5bc2-5cd1-9baa-bd8b990c97fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562861}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562861} :answer-field/id #uuid "131a6720-5179-5e6b-8f36-e30376510b3e" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562857} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "58588f5a-9b68-55e3-be19-a5e5b6a4cf7f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562873} {:answer/id #uuid "9feee51e-8401-51e5-96ac-227b7313667d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562893}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562893} :answer-field/id #uuid "45d82d62-d901-5b62-a460-0db146091d33" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562866} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "783b131e-8f12-50a4-83d7-9f8aaca679d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562880} {:answer/id #uuid "b095e79b-a819-586b-ab09-7239d584f9f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562897}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562897} :answer-field/id #uuid "5e7a67a5-a17a-53dc-81ea-712acf4793d9" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562874}] :question/id #uuid "8c1748bb-90d6-5563-8ef1-b046b936907d" :question/problem "$$\nO=\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & -9 & -4 & -6 & -4\\end{bmatrix},\\,P=\\begin{bmatrix}9 & -4 & -2 \\\\ -5 & 8 & -9 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,R=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the matrices $O,P,$ and $R?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The product $OR$ is well defined\n\n- **II.** The product $OP$ is well defined\n\n- **III.** The product $RO$ is well defined" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $O$ is a $1\\times 5$ row vector, $P$ is a $4\\times 3$ matrix, and $R$ is a $3\\times 1$ column vector.\n\nThere are $5$ columns in $O$ and $3$ rows in $R.$ Since the number of columns in $O$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $R,$ the matrices $O$ and $R$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{O}_{1\\times 5}{\\times }_{\\ne }{R}_{3\\times 1}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there are $5$ columns in $O$ and $4$ rows in $P.$ Since the number of columns in $O$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $P,$ the matrices $O$ and $P$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{O}_{1\\times 5}{\\times }_{\\ne }{P}_{4\\times 3}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nFinally, there is $1$ column in $R$ and $1$ row in $O.$ Since the number of columns in $R$ equals the number of rows in $O,$ the matrices $R$ and $O$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{R}_{3\\times \\boxed{\\text{1}}}{\\times }_{✓}{O}_{\\boxed{\\text{1}}\\times 5}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nTherefore, statement III is true, while statements I and II are false."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562889 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c6a813dd-19f7-54e1-a2c7-bd667d5aed30" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562903} {:answer/id #uuid "e19500d1-8755-5dc6-ac50-746ede9424ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562915}] :answer-field/correc